<title>USA: Comair June load factor 64.4 pct vs 60.9.</title>
<headline>Comair June load factor 64.4 pct vs 60.9.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>JUNE</p>
<p>				1997	     1996	    % Change</p>
<p>    ASMs (000)	   245,675	  221,313	     11.0%</p>
<p>    RPMs (000)	   158,150	  134,687	     17.4%</p>
<p>    LOAD FACTOR	     64.4%	    60.9%	     5.8%</p>
<p>    PASSENGERS	   466,739	  413,389	     12.9%</p>
<p>					 FISCAL YTD</p>
<p>				1998	     1997	    % Change</p>
<p>    ASMs (000)	   746,657	  672,541	     11.0%</p>
<p>    RPMs (000)	   458,995	  392,293	     17.0%</p>
<p>    LOAD FACTOR	     61.5%	    58.3%	     5.4%</p>
<p>    PASSENGERS	 1,367,119	1,202,041	     13.7%</p>
<p>					  CALENDAR YTD</p>
<p>				1997	     1996	    % Change</p>
<p>    ASMs (000)	 1,463,694	1,292,146	     13.3%</p>
<p>    RPMs (000)	   836,197	  733,172	     14.1%</p>
<p>    LOAD FACTOR	     57.1%	    56.7%	     0.7%</p>
<p>    PASSENGERS	  2,515,466	2,292,686		9.7%</p>
<p>Note: The company's full name is Comair Holdings Inc, parent of Comair Inc.</p>
<p>The company said much of the increase in passengers is due to an increase in leisure passengers traveling at discounted fares.</p>
</text>
